  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "Simplify the expression $[\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta -\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta ]^{9}.$",
  "worked_solution": "For expressions involving subtraction, De Moivre's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{[\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\phi )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\phi )]}^{n}=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(n\\phi )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(n\\phi ).\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=9$ and $\\phi =\\theta .$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta -\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta ]^{9} & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(9\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(9\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
